'''Alumini de Balboa, S.A.''' ({{lang|ca|Alumini de Balboa}}) is a Balboan primary aluminium smelting company and the flagship of the country's domestic processing chain for non-ferrous metals. The company operates smelting facilities in the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] foothills of [[Jala Province|Jala]], powered by hydroelectric dams on the Yalabirga rivers. Founded in 1974 as part of the [[Balboan People's Party|BPP]] government's post-reunification industrialisation strategy, Alumini de Balboa converts bauxite — sourced from domestic mines in the Yalabirga range and imported from [[Potocsí]] and [[Tapuya]] via [[Recursos del Marañón]] — into alumina and primary aluminium ingots for both the domestic market and export.

The company is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker ALB. The Government of Balboa retains a 15 per cent stake, reflecting the strategic importance of aluminium production to the domestic processing chain. [[CIEA]] holds an 8 per cent stake, reflecting the energy-intensive nature of aluminium smelting and the integration of energy and metals in the Badia Curta industrial complex. The [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] holds a 5 per cent stake.

